<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maragtas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1907</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Maragtas is a book published in 1907 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-monteclaro">Pedro Monteclaro</a> in Iloilo, setting out a legendary history of Panay drawn from oral tradition. It tells of ten datus from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> who bought land from the Ati and founded settlements on the island. Historians such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-henry-scott">William Henry Scott</a> have shown that it is not a pre-Spanish document, though it remains important in Visayan identity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maragtas.jpg" alt="Maragtas" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Boxer Codex · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naturales_4.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
